# =========================
# Sample runtime output
# =========================
#
# Samples/02_Sprite generates its demo image next to whatever directory it is
# launched from, so running it out of the repo root leaves a Loose/ behind. The
# image is regenerated whenever it is missing.
Loose/

# =========================
# The source tree is never build output
# =========================
#
# Everything above came from the original Visual Studio / C# era template. Those
# patterns carry no path prefix, so they match at any depth — and they match
# directory names that C++ projects legitimately use for source. Four have been
# swallowed silently so far:
#
#   [Bb]in/     -> bgfx/tools/bin/      (dxcompiler.dll, shaderc's DXIL backend)
#   [Bb]uild/   -> DirectXMath/build/   (its CMake packaging templates)
#   build-*/    -> SDL3/build-scripts/
#   [Dd]ebug/   -> Source/RE/Debug/     (the whole RE_Debug module, M1)
#
# Builds are always out of source (CMakePresets pins binaryDir to Build/), so
# nothing under Source/ is ever build output. Exempt the entire tree rather than
# playing whack-a-mole with directory names as modules get added.
#
# Keep this rule last: git applies the last matching pattern.
!/Source/**
!/viewer/third_party/**

__pycache__/
export/
cdn/